WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:18.268
The marionette master packed his wagon quickly so he could steal Pinocchio and leave town.

2
00:00:18.269 --> 00:00:26.853
Because he was in a hurry, he threw his money bag, tools, and tent in a pile on top of Pinocchio's cage.

3
00:00:26.854 --> 00:00:31.675
As the wagon drove on, the heaviest bags fell next to Pinocchio.

4
00:00:31.676 --> 00:00:37.000
By now Pinocchio had stopped crying, though he was still very sad.

5
00:00:37.001 --> 00:00:41.978
He felt the wagon bump and jerk, but could only see bags.

6
00:00:41.979 --> 00:00:47.282
"Hmm, I wonder what's in these bags?" he thought.

7
00:00:47.283 --> 00:00:51.600
"There must be something here that will help me escape."

8
00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:57.990
He stretched his arm out of the cage as far as it would go and opened the first bag quietly.

9
00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.561
He reached his hand into the bag.

10
00:01:00.562 --> 00:01:03.768
"Oh! This bag is full of coins!

11
00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:07.176
There must be a hundred lire in here!"

12
00:01:07.177 --> 00:01:09.519
He pulled some of the coins into his cage.

13
00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:15.991
Much to his surprise, the coins weren't lire—they were pure gold!

14
00:01:15.992 --> 00:01:17.832
"I'll be rich!

15
00:01:17.833 --> 00:01:21.012
Now I can buy Geppetto a coat!

16
00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:25.758
Oh, but these coins won't help me get out of this cage.

17
00:01:25.759 --> 00:01:28.523
I must keep looking."

18
00:01:28.524 --> 00:01:30.849
He was careful to move quietly.

19
00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:33.677
He reached into the second bag.

20
00:01:33.678 --> 00:01:38.510
"Hmm. This bag has too many different kinds of objects.

21
00:01:38.511 --> 00:01:41.077
I can't tell what any of these are.

22
00:01:41.078 --> 00:01:45.627
Let me pull them out one by one.

23
00:01:45.628 --> 00:01:49.586
A whistle? No, that won't help.

24
00:01:49.587 --> 00:01:53.427
A spoon? No, that won't help.

25
00:01:53.428 --> 00:01:57.433
A book? No, that won't help.

26
00:01:57.434 --> 00:02:03.624
Some matches? Hmm. I have an idea."

27
00:02:03.625 --> 00:02:07.535
Pinocchio waited for the wagon to stop.

28
00:02:07.536 --> 00:02:12.833
Quickly, he took the book, wrapped it around his leg, and lit the book on fire.

29
00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:15.407
Then, he threw the match into the wagon.

30
00:02:15.408 --> 00:02:20.454
"Help!" he shouted. "Fire! I'm on fire!"

31
00:02:20.455 --> 00:02:27.552
The marionette master heard Pinocchio cry for help, and he could smell something burning.

32
00:02:27.553 --> 00:02:32.823
He ran to the back of the wagon and began to unpack quickly, trying to find the fire.

33
00:02:32.824 --> 00:02:43.421
When he reached Pinocchio's cage, he grabbed the cage, unlocked it, pulled Pinocchio out, and covered his leg with a blanket so the fire would stop.

34
00:02:43.422 --> 00:02:45.908
"Look, there's more fire!"

35
00:02:45.909 --> 00:02:48.209
Pinocchio pointed to the wagon.

36
00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:51.884
"Oh no! My tent is on fire!"

37
00:02:51.885 --> 00:02:55.757
the man screamed, and he hurried to put the fire out.

38
00:02:55.758 --> 00:03:04.678
While the marionette master was trying to save his tent, Pinocchio snuck out from under the blanket and ran into the nearby woods.

39
00:03:04.679 --> 00:03:11.893
By the time the fire was put out, Pinocchio was long gone, but he could hear the man yelling in the distance,

40
00:03:11.894 --> 00:03:16.894
"No! Wait! Pinocchio, please come back!

41
00:03:16.895 --> 00:03:19.797
I will make you a star!"

42
00:03:19.798 --> 00:03:23.711
Pinocchio ran and ran and ran.

43
00:03:23.712 --> 00:03:27.931
But no matter how hard he ran, nothing looked familiar.

44
00:03:27.932 --> 00:03:31.928
Pinocchio stopped running and sat down on a stump to think.

45
00:03:31.929 --> 00:03:34.413
"I'm lost!" he cried.

46
00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:38.365
"I can't find the village and I don't know what to do.

47
00:03:38.366 --> 00:03:42.710
Oh, someone, please help me!"

48
00:03:42.711 --> 00:03:47.573
What Pinocchio didn't realize is that there are many creatures in the woods.

49
00:03:47.574 --> 00:03:53.419
Some are honest and good, and others are greedy.
